import{_ as t,o,c as i,a2 as a}from"./chunks/framework.DGk0zlJw.js";const p=JSON.parse('{"title":"todo 42-item triage (2026-10-16 user order)","description":"","frontmatter":{},"headers":[],"relativePath":"todo-triage-2026-10-16.md","filePath":"todo-triage-2026-10-16.md"}'),n={name:"todo-triage-2026-10-16.md"};function s(d,e,r,c,l,h){return o(),i("div",null,[...e[0]||(e[0]=[a('<h1 id="todo-42-item-triage-2026-10-16-user-order" tabindex="-1">todo 42-item triage (2026-10-16 user order) <a class="header-anchor" href="#todo-42-item-triage-2026-10-16-user-order" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;todo 42-item triage (2026-10-16 user order)&quot;">​</a></h1><blockquote><p><strong>Historical snapshot, archive only</strong> (DOC-01): the line numbers below are <code>todo.md</code> line numbers as of 2026-10-16 and have since drifted with new entries; do not dispatch work by them. The current authoritative ledger is the repo-root <code>todo.md</code> (outside the docs tree, so not a served link here); judge by item text. Criteria: classify each of the 42 unchecked items in <code>todo.md</code> into A (implementable directly) / B (needs the user&#39;s environment or a user decision) / C (already proxy-verified, can be closed). Red line per the order: a C-class checkoff must cite evidence (scenario name or a test file at <code>file:line</code>); no checkoffs to clear the ledger. This version&#39;s conclusion is <strong>C is the empty set</strong> — rationale in the next section. The 6 items the user named (37/39/57/62/65/67) do carry「已代验」 in their parentheses, but each parenthesis also retains its own「需装机半」(installation half) — and per the acceptance criteria todo.md sets for itself (&quot;a change that was not verified does not count as done&quot;), checkoff would be self-contradictory. All 6 go to B, with their proxy-verified halves listed separately in the B table along with the matching installation-checklist row. Line numbers refer to <code>todo.md</code> as of this document&#39;s creation; adding or removing todo rows shifts them, so judge by the item text itself.</p></blockquote><h2 id="overview" tabindex="-1">Overview <a class="header-anchor" href="#overview" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Overview&quot;">​</a></h2><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>Class</th><th>Count</th><th>Distribution</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>A implementable directly</td><td>5</td><td>All of Phase 5「完善组件目录与用户体验」(todo.md:184-188)</td></tr><tr><td>B needs the user&#39;s environment or a user decision</td><td>37</td><td>MVP 21 (:37-83) + 后续可选 1 (:91) + 验收 3 (:96-99) + the 6 Phase 4 rows (:175-180, need a decision) + the 6 Phase 6 rows (:192-197, real-machine acceptance)</td></tr><tr><td>C already proxy-verified, can be closed</td><td>0</td><td>No single item meets &quot;evidence covering the whole row&quot;</td></tr></tbody></table><h2 id="why-c-is-the-empty-set" tabindex="-1">Why C is the empty set <a class="header-anchor" href="#why-c-is-the-empty-set" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Why C is the empty set&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Criterion: for an item to qualify for C, the existing proxy evidence must cover the row&#39;s <strong>entire</strong> acceptance criteria. Checking them one by one:</p><ol><li>The parentheses of all 21 unchecked MVP items end with「需装机半」, and most additionally depend on real credentials (:44/:46/:48/:54/:99), physical hardware (:70/:71), or OS-surface behavior (:37/:57/:96/:97). The CI evidence (<code>daily-build</code> visual-evidence artifacts; a failed assertion is a red build) covers only the mechanical half.</li><li>The 6 items the user named are the best-evidenced group, and still do not cover their whole rows: <ul><li>todo.md:37 the process half is proxy-verified (scenario E1, process count stays 1); the wake bubble is an OS Toast surface (E1b probe built, degrades to warning when invisible in a headless session, run 38619441591).</li><li>todo.md:39 position restore + the drag gesture chain are proxy-verified (scenarios R/R3, run 38750239155); cross-DPI topology needs physical multiple monitors.</li><li>todo.md:57 the AUMID self-heal half is proxy-verified (scenario F5t, <code>Initialize()</code> rebuilds after the registry key is pre-deleted, run 38494525200); click/activation routing is an OS Toast surface.</li><li>todo.md:62 cache-without-white-screen + Esc keyboard close are proxy-verified (scenario K3 hard assertion, run 38743014862); precise 100ms timing needs a stopwatch.</li><li>todo.md:65 the blank-area hit-test ruling is proxy-verified (H5b <code>WM_NCHITTEST</code>: tile row = HTCLIENT, outer blank band = HTTRANSPARENT, run 38750239155); how a real mouse click lands on the window below is an installation-side impression.</li><li>todo.md:67 position restore + either/or + the drag chain are proxy-verified (scenarios H/H6, run 38750239155); drag feel needs an installation.</li></ul></li><li>Engine-level evidence is indeed complete (<code>tests/Beacon.Core.Tests/EventBusTests.cs:9</code> Publish_InvokesAllSubscribers, <code>:25</code> HandlerException_DoesNotAffectOtherSubscribers, <code>:38</code> Unsubscribe_StopsDelivery, <code>:52</code> publish snapshot semantics, <code>:86</code> SubscribeOnUi_MarshalsToDispatcher; <code>tests/Beacon.Core.Tests/NotificationEngineTests.cs</code> engine de-duplication and cooldown), but those items are consumed by rows todo.md already has checked (:58/:59) and do not sit among the 42 unchecked.</li></ol><p>Conclusion: checkoff-ing the 6 items to clear the ledger would violate both the order&#39;s red line and todo.md&#39;s own acceptance criteria, so it is not done. If you consider the installation half of one of them droppable (e.g. downgrade &quot;bubble impression&quot; or &quot;100ms timing&quot; to out of scope), that is a change of acceptance criteria — say so explicitly and I will check it off under the new criteria with a note.</p><h2 id="class-a-5-items-phase-5-refining-the-component-catalog-and-user-experience" tabindex="-1">Class A (5 items): Phase 5 refining the component catalog and user experience <a class="header-anchor" href="#class-a-5-items-phase-5-refining-the-component-catalog-and-user-experience" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Class A (5 items): Phase 5 refining the component catalog and user experience&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Baseline facts: Phase 2 already prepared the design tokens and vocabulary components (<code>ComponentFeedback</code> — the four vocabulary components Empty/Loading/Error/Offline — is landed but has no call sites; see <code>docs/design/redesign-2026-10-16-组件库落地.md</code>; <code>SampleGalleryWindow</code> already has live specimens of all 14 factories), so class A is mainly <strong>wiring already-prepared components onto real surfaces</strong>, not building new ones from scratch.</p><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>Row</th><th>Item</th><th>Implementation points</th><th>Local gate</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>187</td><td>Unified empty / offline / error states</td><td>Wire the four <code>ComponentFeedback</code> components into the QuickPanel empty areas and the Detail no-data state, replacing today&#39;s two competing conventions (&quot;empty area hidden&quot; + &quot;XAML banner&quot;); after wiring, delete the duplicate text branches</td><td>No Core pure-function change, so no new unit tests; App side hand-audited + CI</td></tr><tr><td>185</td><td>Richer layout and conditional display</td><td>Add call sites for the <code>ComponentLayout</code> Column vocabulary component beyond the existing Row/Columns/SectionLabel/When; drive conditional display from state fields rather than hard-coding it</td><td>Layout invariants are already guarded (<code>ComponentLayerInvariantTests</code>); add one case for the new shape</td></tr><tr><td>184</td><td>Timeline, table, chart and trend components</td><td>Add three component factories (timeline over event history, table over multi-row payload, chart over trend series); data flows through the existing binding engine (state / selector / const three states) with no new Provider</td><td>One set of Core-side parse and empty-state tests each</td></tr><tr><td>186</td><td>Component instance editing, sizing and desktop layout configuration</td><td>Add an instance surface to the settings page (component-tree editing, size tier, desktop layout region); writes go through the existing <code>Config.UpsertWidget</code> + tree-validation fail-closed convention</td><td>Add Storage-side tests for the validation branches</td></tr><tr><td>188</td><td>Theme, density and accessibility refinement</td><td>Wire a density scale (compact/regular) into the <code>DesignTokens</code> spacing scale; fill in accessibility — UIA names and focus order (current known pitfall: a Border with only AutomationId does not enter the UIA tree, <code>SetName</code> is required to create a peer)</td><td>After UIA names are filled, scenario X-class assertions need a matching recheck</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Priority order: 187 → 185 → 184 → 186 → 188. Rationale: 187 is pure wiring with no new semantics, lowest risk; 185 depends on 187&#39;s state semantics; 184&#39;s three new components have the largest surface but are purely additive; 186 touches the settings page and the configuration surface (widest change blast radius, so later); 188&#39;s accessibility fill-in should happen after the new surfaces of the previous four are settled, otherwise it is rework.</p><p><strong>Blocker (this machine is Linux)</strong>: the App side (<code>src/Beacon.App/</code>, WinUI 3) cannot be built on Linux — <code>XamlCompiler</code> dies before <code>Csc</code>, so there is no local C# gate; App changes are only hand-audited here and validated by CI (<code>windows-latest</code>). Core / Storage unit tests can run locally in full. This does not block delivery; it is the established delivery path — every previous App change landed this way.</p><h2 id="class-b-37-items-what-the-user-needs-to-provide" tabindex="-1">Class B (37 items): what the user needs to provide <a class="header-anchor" href="#class-b-37-items-what-the-user-needs-to-provide" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Class B (37 items): what the user needs to provide&quot;">​</a></h2><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>Needed from the user</th><th>Rows covered</th><th>Exactly what is missing</th><th>Proxy-verified half (evidence)</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>A real GitHub PAT</td><td>44, 46, 48, 54, 99</td><td>A revocable real PAT + a real repository with PR and Actions activity</td><td>mock chain scenario D; API-layer fake-Handler unit tests (GitHubPullRequestsProviderTests 18, GitHubActionsProviderTests 9, GitHubApiClientTests 10, GitHubWorkflowExecutorTests 6); mapping layer table-driven</td></tr><tr><td>A real vendor API and its credential fields</td><td>91</td><td>The vendor-private packaging tool&#39;s API docs, credential field names, and quota conventions</td><td>The Jenkins Provider on an open standard API is already landed (<code>jenkins.build</code>)</td></tr><tr><td>Installation-side impression / timing / audio inspection</td><td>37, 52, 57, 60, 62, 65, 67, 73, 75, 79, 80, 97</td><td>A headed desktop session: bubble/Toast presentation, default-browser navigation, a stopwatch for the 100ms check, listening, tray-icon inspection, drag feel</td><td>E1 process half, F5t AUMID self-heal half, K3 Esc keyboard close, H1 foreground unchanged, H5b <code>WM_NCHITTEST</code> hit-test ruling, G7a tile-layer reflection, G4/G5 color change, G6/G7b/G7c/V2 four pulse halves, V1/V2/V4 injection and notification chain (runs in each parenthesis)</td></tr><tr><td>Physical or virtual display stack (multiple monitors, different DPI, hot-plug)</td><td>39, 70, 71</td><td>At least two monitors at different scales; CI is a single-monitor session and cannot drive topology events</td><td>R/R3 position and drag chain, H/H6 floating drag and restore (run 38750239155)</td></tr><tr><td>A real human end-to-end walk</td><td>74, 82, 83</td><td>A clean Windows 11 VM + a recording; the RFC §6.2.7 four items involve a real network and human steps</td><td>Screenshots already archived in the <code>visual-evidence</code> artifacts; the cache hydration full-cycle unit test has passed</td></tr><tr><td>A user decision (the HTML boundary ruling)</td><td>175, 176, 177, 178, 179, 180</td><td>Phase 4 must get an architecture decision before starting: the repo holds a countervailing record (<code>docs/master-plan.md:769</code>), and about 60% of the design draft&#39;s claims about &quot;existing implementation&quot; do exist in the repo while two of its underlying premises are largely absent</td><td>None (no code before the decision)</td></tr><tr><td>Real-machine regression acceptance</td><td>192, 193, 194, 195, 196, 197</td><td>Depends on class A landing + the Phase 4 ruling, then the 71-item installation checklist and scenario-evidence regression</td><td>The 71-item installation checklist is in place (<code>docs/acceptance-checklist.md</code>), and CI visual-evidence scenarios A-Z are already the regression gate</td></tr></tbody></table><h2 id="sync-convention-with-todo-md" tabindex="-1">Sync convention with todo.md <a class="header-anchor" href="#sync-convention-with-todo-md" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Sync convention with todo.md&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li>This document does not check off any todo row (C is the empty set).</li><li>Class B rows are left verbatim (their parentheses already carry &quot;proxy-verified half + installation half&quot;, consistent with the B table here).</li><li>Class A is implemented one item at a time in priority order; after each item lands, its commit hash is appended to the matching <code>todo.md</code> parenthesis and it is checked off, on the same convention as Phase 0-3.</li><li>When an installation half clears, the matching date annotation in <code>docs/acceptance-checklist.md</code> is updated in sync.</li></ul>',17)])])}const m=t(n,[["render",s]]);export{p as __pageData,m as default};
